  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(-1) & \u2248\\frac{f(-1)-f(-1-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(-1)-f(-2)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1-0.4}{1} \\\\  & =-0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
